  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe [\"scroll to the fragment\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#scroll-to-the-fragment-identifier) algorithm runs the [ancestor revealing algorithm](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#ancestor-revealing-algorithm) in step 3.4, then unconditionally proceeds to scroll (3.5), focus (3.6), and move the sequential focus navigation starting point (3.7) using *target*.\n\nThe ancestor revealing algorithm can run script via the `beforematch` event (step 4.2.2). Script can remove *target* from the document during that event. The ancestor revealing algorithm itself handles this internally: step 4.2.3 checks if `ancestorToReveal` is connected after firing `beforematch`, but the caller (\"scroll to the fragment\") does not re-check *target* after the algorithm returns.\n\nThis means steps 3.5–3.7 can operate on a *target* that is no longer connected to *document*. Additionally, step 3.3 sets *document*'s target element to *target* before the algorithm runs, but never clears it if *target* is removed, leaving stale `:target` state.\n\ncc @emilio @josepharhar ",
